semgrep ci --no-suppress-errors with --allow-local-builds: when dependency resolution fails and the scan exits with code 2, the reason is now also in the `errors` of the JSON output (one entry per resolver error or lockfile parse error of each failed subproject, or a generic entry if none was reported; resolver errors include the failed command and the end of its output, with common credential shapes such as URL credentials and Authorization headers redacted), not only in the log. Previously the JSON had no error, so pipelines that read it could not tell why the scan failed.
